# Shell scripts must reach the Docker image with LF endings.
#
# Real incident, 2026-08-21: a deploy failed with
# `env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory`. The committed blob was
# genuinely LF, but this is a Windows dev machine with core.autocrlf=true,
# so the working-tree copy of docker-entrypoint.sh had CRLF -- and CRLF in
# a shebang breaks it. The image is built from the working tree, not from
# the commit, so a clean repository is no protection.
#
# It was also invisible to the usual pre-deploy check: `docker run ...
# python -c "import combined_bot"` passes, because that bypasses
# ENTRYPOINT entirely.
*.sh text eol=lf
docker-entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
